  298:           # "non-closing" words are NOT safe: ref, part of, related to, towards all do it.
  299:           # A CLOSING verb additionally closes the item, which is louder but not separate.
  300:           #
  301:           # This guard therefore fails on ANY id the branch does not own, not only on ids beside
  302:           # a closing verb. An earlier version checked only the verb and told authors to reach
  303:           # for `ref`/`towards` instead â€” advice that caused the exact defect it was preventing.
  304:           # Refer to other items IN WORDS: "the item that landed the relay".
  305:           #
  306:           # The hazard punishes good practice â€” the better the write-up, the more items it cites,
  307:           # and the most-cited item is the one somebody is actively working. Nothing checked that
  308:           # the pull request had any relationship to the item it closed, which is the same
